From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: derive a stable factory MAC address from the SoC serial
 number

The WCN6855 on the Huawei MateBook E Go has no programmed MAC address.
The firmware hands out 00:03:7f:12:xx:xx with the last two bytes random
on every boot, and ath11k reports it as the permanent address, which is
what WifiIfaceUtil::getFactoryMacAddress() returns. When connected MAC
randomization is enabled and a network uses the device MAC, the
framework sets the interface to this factory MAC before connecting, so
the address cannot be made stable from userspace alone.

Derive the address from /sys/devices/soc0/serial_number: the low six
bytes of FNV-1a 64 over "gaokun3-wifi-mac:<interface>:<serial>", with
the locally administered bit set and the multicast bit cleared. Each
interface gets its own fixed address. Fall back to the permanent
address when the serial number cannot be read. hal_wifi can already
read all sysfs types. The device overlay sets
config_wifiSaveFactoryMacToWifiConfigStore to false, so the framework
does not keep using an address it stored earlier.

The device overlay currently disables connected MAC randomization, so
the framework does not set the interface address before connecting.
device/huawei/gaokun3/bin/gaokun3-wlan-ap.sh therefore writes the same
derived address to wlan0 at boot; the two implementations must stay
identical.

The serial number is 32 bits wide and can be recovered from the
address by brute force. It is not a secret; the hash only keeps it out
of the address in plain form.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific]
---
 wifi/aidl/default/wifi_iface_util.cpp | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wifi/aidl/default/wifi_iface_util.cpp b/wifi/aidl/default/wifi_iface_util.cpp
index 536812c..c06db19 100644
--- a/wifi/aidl/default/wifi_iface_util.cpp
+++ b/wifi/aidl/default/wifi_iface_util.cpp
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@
 
 #include <android-base/logging.h>
 #include <android-base/macros.h>
+#include <android-base/file.h>
+#include <android-base/strings.h>
 #include <net/if.h>
 #include <private/android_filesystem_config.h>
 
@@ -31,6 +33,30 @@ namespace {
 constexpr uint8_t kMacAddressMulticastMask = 0x01;
 constexpr uint8_t kMacAddressLocallyAssignedMask = 0x02;
 
+// Stable locally administered "factory" MAC derived from the SoC serial number. The board
+// has no programmed MAC, and the firmware hands out 00:03:7f:12:xx:xx with the last two
+// bytes random on every boot.
+bool gaokun3StableMac(const std::string& iface_name, std::array<uint8_t, 6>* mac) {
+    std::string serial;
+    if (!::android::base::ReadFileToString("/sys/devices/soc0/serial_number", &serial)) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    serial = ::android::base::Trim(serial);
+    if (serial.empty() || serial == "0") return false;
+    const std::string key = "gaokun3-wifi-mac:" + iface_name + ":" + serial;
+    uint64_t h = 0xcbf29ce484222325ULL;  // FNV-1a 64
+    for (unsigned char c : key) {
+        h ^= c;
+        h *= 0x100000001b3ULL;
+    }
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < mac->size(); i++) {
+        (*mac)[i] = static_cast<uint8_t>(h >> (8 * i));
+    }
+    (*mac)[0] &= ~kMacAddressMulticastMask;
+    (*mac)[0] |= kMacAddressLocallyAssignedMask;
+    return true;
+}
+
 #ifdef WIFI_HAL_RETRY_SET_MAC_ADDRESS
 // Constants to retry within setMacAddress()
 constexpr uint32_t kMaxSetMacAddressRetries = 5;
@@ -52,6 +78,8 @@ WifiIfaceUtil::WifiIfaceUtil(const std::weak_ptr<::android::wifi_system::Interfa
       event_handlers_map_() {}
 
 std::array<uint8_t, 6> WifiIfaceUtil::getFactoryMacAddress(const std::string& iface_name) {
+    std::array<uint8_t, 6> stable_mac;
+    if (gaokun3StableMac(iface_name, &stable_mac)) return stable_mac;
     return iface_tool_.lock()->GetFactoryMacAddress(iface_name.c_str());
 }
 
